            "Problem": [
                "How fast is the area of a square increasing when the side is `%side% %lenunit%` and growing at a rate of `%ds/dt% (%lenunit%)/(%timeunit%)`?"
            ],
            "Answer": ["`%dA/dt% (%lenunit%^2)/(%timeunit%)`"],
            "Explanation": [
                "<span class='sep'>Step 1: Gather info</span>",
                "`ds/dt = %ds/dt% (%lenunit%)/(%timeunit%)`",
                "`s = %side% %lenunit%`",
                "Looking for `dA/dt`",
                "<span class='sep'>Step 2: Find an equation that connects the 2 variables</span>",
                "`A = s^2`",
                "<span class='sep'>Step 3: Take the derivative of both side relative to t</span>",
                "`(d)/(dt)[A] = (d)/(dt)[s^2]`",
                "`(dA)/(dt) = 2s(ds)/(dt)`",
                "<span class='sep'>Step 4: Plug in information</span>",
                "`(dA)/(dt) = 2(%side%)(%ds/dt%)`",
                "<span class='sep'>Step 5: Solve</span>",
                "`(dA)/(dt) = %dA/dt% ((%lenunit%)^2)/(%timeunit%)`"
            ]
        },
